            "review_title": "Review at Hanayuki Dao Tan",
            "review_text": "CGL_17\nSingapore, Singapore97 contributions\n0\ngood, fresh seafood\nAug 2018\nThe seafood sashimi served at Hanayuki was really fresh and delicious. They offer a large variety of raw seafood in their menu. You can order a mix platter of seafood sashimi which includes the likes of tuna, salmon, yellowtail, etc. Presentation of their dishes were beautiful as with many Japanese restaurants. At Hanayuki, you will be offered crispy sheets of seaweed which can be used to wrap the raw fish seafood. This is the first time I have eaten sashimi wrapped with seawood and it does taste good. A must try at the restaurant is the salmon head hotpot. The cut-up pieces of slamon head are cooked with vegetables and tofu in the hotpot, making this a really nice meal.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 26, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
