            "review_text": "Van Thanh T\nHanoi, Vietnam215 contributions\n0\nNot the best, but OK\nApr 2013 • Family\nI visit Japanese restaurants in Hanoi occasionally, and for this one these are my points:\n\n- Private rooms, although a bit small but good enough for groups of 2-3 persons. Each has its own air-conditioner. (+1) \n\n- The price is a bit less expensive than some other Japanese restaurants. (+1)\n\n- Dishes are quite OK, compared to those of more costly restaurants. (+1)\n\n- Parking space available. (+1)\n\n- Offer welcome fruit drinks. (+1)\n\n- Outside the rooms, staff chatting loud at times. (-1). Compared to other Japanese restaurants in Hanoi, their service is not bad, but certainly not the best.\n\nOverall, they deserve 4-star of of 5.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 11, 2013",
